  "query_preview": "..\n(This afternoon through next Saturday)\nIssued at 1146 AM CDT Sun Oct 18 2026\n\nYet another beautiful, fall-like day is progressing across the\nMid-South with plenty of sunshine and temperatures in the upper\n50s to low 60s. Surface high pressure is expected to remain\nthrough the upcoming work week, with a weak upper-level ridge\naloft eventually giving way to generally northwesterly flow by\nthe middle of the week. A dry forecast will continue as a result,\nwith no precipitation in the forecast for the foreseeable future.\nAs far as temperatures go, temperatures will gradually warm and\nreturn to above-normal by the middle of the week. Expect for high\ntemperatures to be back into the 70s on Monday, rising to the\nupper 70s to 80s Wednesday onward. Overnight lows will remain\naround to just below normal though, generally in the 40s with\nsome locations creeping back into the 50s by Wednesday morning.\nThe only concern weather wise for the upcoming week will be the\nthreat for elevated fire danger. With the little rainfall we have\nreceived, persistent drought conditions, and relatively low\nrelative humidity, outdoor burning and activities that involve\nopen sparks or flames are discouraged. Please heed to any local\nburn bans through the upcoming week.",
